WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Thanks for tuning into SpaceX Daily Episode 9, I'm Patrick in Vancouver,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.740
today is June 20th, 2026. Here's what's happening at SpaceX today.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.960
Meccazilla upgrades at Starbase move the next booster catch attempt, one step closer by refining

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.800
the tower arms that must absorb a returning Starship's full mass and velocity. SpaceX is

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.180
actively updating the Meccazilla tower arms and catch hardware at Starbase. The work directly

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.980
supports the ongoing Starship flight test campaign that last flew on June 19th.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.800
Refined arm positioning and load bearing capacity address the central open question of

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.980
reliable booster capture on every flight. Listeners should watch for static fire or fit check

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:49.260
milestones in the coming days that confirm the new geometry. Remember the show covered Starship

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:55.960
on June 19th, today's refinements move that capture goal forward by tightening the hardware variables

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:02.020
that matter most for a repeatable return. While the tower team works the hardest capture problem

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.820
in aerospace, another vehicle is preparing to test an entirely different return architecture.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.420
SpaceX will fly a disc-shaped capsule on Tuesday to test in-space manufacturing hardware.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:20.260
The vehicle targets production of materials that benefit from sustained microgravity and vacuum

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:26.400
conditions. Success would move the open question of orbital refueling and on-orbit assembly,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:33.080
one step forward by proving a reusable return architecture. The shallow wide profile lowers

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:39.040
peak heat flux during reentry while opening more internal volume for payloads than a traditional

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.560
cylinder would allow on the same faring. As Starfall explores new orbital hardware,

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.280
the workhorse Falcon 9 keeps the constellation growing at a steady cadence.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:55.720
A Falcon 9 is scheduled to lift 24 Starlink satellites from Vandenberg Space Force Base

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:05.040
Pad 4E at 8.12 a.m. Pacific Daylight Time Today. The Starlink 17-28 mission marks the 58th

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:10.900
dedicated broadband launch into low Earth orbit. This cadence directly feeds the open question

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:15.740
of annual launch rate ceiling and how quickly the constellation can add capacity.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:23.280
Observers on the spaceflight now live thread noted the window opens at 8.12 a.m. Pacific Daylight Time

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:29.300
and discussed how the mission fits the current two per week pattern. Local California spotters

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:34.100
shared viewing angles for the plan flight from Vandenberg, highlighting clear coastal

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:39.600
sightlines south of the pad. Next big future readers speculated on the nature of an

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.840
imminent SpaceX announcement. The announcement is built as enabling anything anywhere operations.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:52.200
The timeline for those operations is described as within three days. Readers focused on the

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:58.100
announcement as a potential indicator of new operational reach. The discussion occurred among

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:04.260
followers tracking SpaceX progress in real time. Community interest centers on how the announcement

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:10.340
could alter existing mission profiles. RS-Tectica commenters examined the French startup that

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:16.080
quietly dropped its rocket name over trademark concerns. The name change addressed potential

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.640
legal conflicts in the small launch sector. Commenters considered what the move signals for

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.400
competitive positioning among smaller vehicles. The startup's decision drew attention to trademark

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:32.840
issues affecting new entrants. Discussion highlighted implications for the broader small

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:38.380
launch market landscape. The same production line that supports commercial broadband also

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:44.980
carries national security payloads. SpaceX previously lofted a batch of national reconnaissance

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:51.180
office star shield satellites from Vandenberg on June 19th. The mission expands the dedicated

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:56.580
military constellation that shares the Falcon 9 production line with commercial starlink flights.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:02.940
Continued star shield cadence tests how far booster reuse limits can be pushed under mixed

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:08.980
manifest pressure. Launch cadence gains also depend on clearing regulatory and legal hurdles

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:15.000
on the ground. The Texas Supreme Court ruled in favor of SpaceX, allowing continued temporary

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:21.780
closures of Boca Chica Beach during launch and test operations. The decision removes a regulatory

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:27.820
constraint that had previously limited pad access windows. It directly supports higher flight cadence

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:32.500
goals for the starship program by preserving operational flexibility at starbase.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:38.840
While operations expand at home, starlink terminals are appearing in unexpected high-profile

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:46.100
platforms. President Trump presented a modified Boeing 747-8 at joint base Andrews that

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:52.540
incorporates starlink terminals for presidential communications. The Qatar gifted aircraft valued

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:59.940
near $400 million serves as an interim platform until the next dedicated VC-25B enters service.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:06.520
The integration demonstrates starlink's expanding role in secure government links beyond commercial

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:13.180
aviation. One thing worth watching is that SpaceX bankers are preparing a potential 20 billion

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:20.040
bond offering according to sources. The size of the rays signals continued heavy capital needs

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:26.080
even after the June 12th public listing. Execution will depend on prevailing credit markets and

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:32.000
whether investors accept the dual-class voting structure already in place. On the AI front,

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:39.120
Justice Department attorneys moved to dismiss the NAACP lawsuit targeting XAI's Memphis data

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:44.380
center turbines, arguing the facility supports national security compute priorities.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:50.820
The filing came days after the same department backed XAI in related environmental proceedings.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:57.240
Pentagon AI leadership separately referenced the cluster in public remarks on domestic compute

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:04.000
capacity. From an engineering standpoint, the disc-shaped Starfall capsule now slated for Tuesday

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.960
flight embodies a deliberate departure from traditional cylindrical reentry vehicles.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:16.100
By adopting a shallow, wide profile, the design lowers peak heat flux during atmospheric entry

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:21.620
while increasing internal volume available for manufacturing payloads. This geometry

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:27.940
trades some packaging efficiency on the Falcon 9 fairing for simpler thermal protection requirements

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:35.180
and a larger usable deck area once on orbit. From first principles, the dominant cost driver in any

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:41.460
orbital manufacturing system is not the raw silicon or metal feedstock, but the energy and mass

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:47.040
penalty of getting that feedstock into a stable microgravity environment and returning finished

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:52.740
product. The disc's blunt body shape produces the idiot index on the thermal protection layer

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:59.120
because fewer tiles are needed per unit of pressurized volume compared with a slender cylinder of

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:05.260
equivalent capacity. If the demo returns even a modest quantity of material produced in vacuum,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.500
it will validate whether the added complexity of a non-cylindrical pressure vessel is offset

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:17.960
by lower per kilogram round trip energy. That single data point will decide whether future

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:23.880
starship tanker flights should prioritize disc class return vehicles or continue refining

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:32.200
conventional cylinder architectures for the same task. And a quick market note, SPCX is at $185

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:40.160
down 5.2% from the prior close. Before we go, watch for the Starfall disc capsule flight on Tuesday

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:46.180
that could validate a new return path for orbital manufacturing. That's the day at SpaceX,

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:55.900
that's a wrap. SPCX is trading at $185 down 5.2%. If you're new here, subscribe,

